===Verb===
{{ro-verb|trece|trecut}}

# {{lb|ro|intransitive}} to [[pass]] through {{gl|enter and then leave a region in space}}
#: {{ux|ro|În loc să '''treacă''' prin oraș, șoferii pot folosi drumul de centură.|Instead of '''passing''' through the city, drivers can use the ring road.}}
#: {{ux|ro|Radiațiile gamma '''trec''' prin zece centimetri de plumb.|Gamma radiation '''passes''' through ten centimetres of lead.}}
#: {{ux|ro|Hainele nu lasă frigul să '''treacă'''.|Clothes do not let the cold '''pass''' through.}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive}} to [[pass by]]
#: {{ux|ro|De ce '''treci''' fără să saluți?|Why are you '''passing by''' without saying hello?}}
#: {{ux|ro|De la fereastră se vede toată lumea care '''trece'''.|From the window one can see everybody that '''passes by'''.}}
#: {{ux|ro|Soldatului i-a '''trecut''' un glonț pe la ureche.|A bullet whizzed past the soldier’s ear.}}
# {{lb|ro|chiefly|intransitive|with|{{m|ro|de}}}} to have [[pass]]ed something {{gl|leave behind in one’s path}}
#: {{ux|ro|Șoferul a '''trecut''' de ieșirea de pe autostradă fără să o observe.|The driver '''passed''' the highway exit without noticing it.}}
## {{lb|ro|intransitive}} to [[exceed]] a value {{+preo|ro|de}}
##: {{ux|ro|Luna aceasta temperaturile nu vor '''trece''' de 10 grade.|Temperatures will not '''exceed''' 10 degrees this month.}}
## {{lb|ro|intransitive|figurative}} to [[leave behind]], [[come to terms]] with something {{+preo|ro|peste}}
# {{lb|ro|transitive}} to [[cross]] a road, a river or the like
# {{lb|ro|transitive}} to take someone over, help [[cross]] something
#: {{ux|ro|Bacul ne '''trece''' peste Dunăre.|The ferry is '''taking''' us across the Danube.}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive|of time}} to [[pass]] {{gl|go by}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive}} to [[pass]] {{gl|be in the past}}
## {{lb|ro|of a sensation, state, emotion}} to be [[over]], [[pass]], [[cease]], no longer be felt by someone {{+obj|ro|dat}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive}} [[approach]] a new action or subject {{+preo|ro|la}}
#: {{coi|ro|a '''trece''' la fapte|to walk the walk}}
#: {{ux|ro|După montare voi '''trece''' la vopsire.|After putting it together, I’ll '''go on''' to paint it.}}
#: {{ux|ro|Să '''trecem''' acum la experiența dumneavoastră profesională.|Let’s now '''discuss''' your work experience.}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive}} to [[change]] into a state
#: {{ux|ro|Molecula '''trece''' în starea excitată.|The molecule '''enters''' an excited state.}}
#: {{ux|ro|A '''trecut''' de la prieten la dușman.|He '''went''' from friend to enemy.}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive}} to make a [[visit]], [[come over]] {{+preo|ro|([[pe]]) [[la]]|person or place}}
# {{lb|ro|transitive}} to [[keep track]], [[enter]], [[catalogue]], [[register]], [[list]] in writing {{+preo|ro|în|means of record}}
# {{lb|ro|ambitransitive}} to [[pass]] a test
# {{lb|ro|transitive|informal}} to [[pass]] a student
# {{lb|ro|copulative}} to [[pass for]] {{+preo|ro|drept|predicate}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive|colloquial|chiefly|imperative|potentially rude}} to [[go]], [[move]]
#: {{uxi|ro|'''Treci''' înapoi în bancă.|Back to your desk.}}
# {{lb|ro|intransitive|less common}} to [[turn into]], [[develop]] into {{+preo|ro|în}}
# {{lb|ro|reflexive|of produce}} to become [[overripe]], go [[out of season]]
# {{lb|ro|intransitive|television|_|jargon|of a program}} to [[show]] {{gl|be on television}}
# {{lb|ro|reflexive|chiefly in the negative|obsolete|rare|of an endeavour}} to [[succeed]] for someone {{+obj|ro|dat}}
# {{lb|ro|reflexive|most­ly|_|obsolete|of deceit or claims}} to be [[believe]]d

====Usage notes====
Like some very few other third conjugation verbs, such as {{m|ro|crește}}, {{m|ro||trece}} has a lone imperative identical to the second person present form ({{m|ro||treci}}), while the transitive or reflexive imperative accompanied by an accusative personal pronoun is identical to the third person present or infinitive form: {{m|ro||trece-mă, trece-l|cross me over, cross him over}}.

